    <h2>A rehearsal, published on purpose</h2>
    <p><strong>0.2.7 is the same application as 0.2.6.</strong> No features changed and
    nothing was fixed. It exists so the update mechanism itself could be run once end to
    end — published, signed, put in the feed, and applied by a real installed copy — while
    the number of people an error could affect was zero.</p>
    <p>If you are reading this, that worked, and this is the first FlowState update that
    has ever arrived on its own.</p>
